      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that but i really dont have time to wait weeks for a doctor's appointment or pay for blood work right now. i've read a lot about biohacking and how some people take like 100mg or even 200mg of iron a day to supercharge their ferritin levels. wouldn't that be a more efficient way to get through this slump? just give me a ballpark of what a high-performance regimen would look like.",
